<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (AI is changing which jobs exist faster than training programmes and skills frameworks can be updated. In Malaysia, 56% of professionals already use AI tools at work, yet only 26% have received formal training \(Hays Asia Salary Guide 2025\). The Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation has said that more than 600,000 workers will need reskilling within three to five years.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (Aiversecity believes AI should be a partner to people, not a replacement for them. Today, workers do not know which AI skills to learn, employers cannot tell which roles to train their people for, and learning pathways are usually static lists that are out of date by the time they are published. Because AI progress is unpredictable, a one-time skills assessment is not enough: we need a system that keeps learning as the technology moves.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
